P1.6: lock CORS, throttle the Basic-auth path, gate auth-disable to loopback

- main.py: replace allow_origins=["*"]+allow_credentials (unsafe and browser-
  ignored) with an explicit allow-list. Prod is same-origin via nginx so the
  grant is unused there; default covers local vite dev. Override with
  INFRADOCS_CORS_ORIGINS (comma-separated).
- dependencies.py: add an in-memory brute-force throttle to the HTTP Basic path
  (10 fails / 5 min / username -> 429). The /login endpoint had a throttle but
  Basic against any endpoint was an unthrottled credential-stuffing channel.
- dependencies.py: INFRADOCS_AUTH_DISABLED is now honored only for a loopback
  caller, so leaving the dev bypass on can't silently expose the API to remote
  clients. Documented the same-host-nginx caveat.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
